// §14 entry 9 -- a HOF passing a row-carrying function where a bare
// function type is expected -> EXS-E0303, not EXS-E0421.
//
// RESTATED against the §8.6/§4.2 reading ratified in commit 4edb704
// (checker.md section 2.1 rule 3, finding 11). The ORIGINAL fixture read a
// bare `functio(f32) -> f32` parameter as an *open* row, so a HOF that
// called its own function-typed parameter `f` without writing `sicut f`
// anywhere in its own `poscit` clause was itself the violation -- "whatever
// `f` turns out to need at a given call site is invisible at THIS
// function's boundary." §8.6 settles it the other way: `poscit {}` is the
// *explicit* empty row, so the unannotated, bare form is the *implicit*
// one, also empty -- not open. Function types then compare by id, rows
// included (checker.md 2.1 rule 3), so `applica_sine_ordine` below, exactly
// as originally written, commits to nothing about `f` beyond "takes no
// capabilities," and calling `f(v)` inside its body is completely
// consistent with that. There is no violation left at its own definition;
// `prototypes/capcheck/cases/bad_hof_no_row.exsc` is the same shape and is
// "not adopted" for the same reason (finding 11).
//
// The attack this entry means to catch still exists, just one step later,
// at a CALL SITE: `identitas_rete` below is an ordinary top-level function
// of type `functio(f32) -> f32 poscit rete` -- a real, non-empty row.
// Passing it where `applica_sine_ordine` declares a bare (empty-row)
// `f: functio(f32) -> f32` is a type mismatch, because the two function
// types are not equal once rows are part of identity: `EXS-E0303`, at the
// `ataca` call site, not `EXS-E0421` at any declaration. This is the
// "poscit rete function where a bare function type is expected" case §14's
// text now names directly.
//
// DEFERRED: needs the type checker (Stage 2) to resolve both function
// types and compare them, not the capability-row checker alone -- this is
// now a class-030x general-typing code, per §13's amendment, not a 042x
// row code. compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both still empty; `exsc
// aedifica`, run directly against this file, exits 0 and reports nothing --
// confirmed, not assumed. §4.2 itself is `[UNTESTED]` as a soundness claim
// beyond a nine-case Python probe (`prototypes/capcheck/`), which CLAUDE.md
// and `prototypes/README.md` both forbid this suite from depending on.

publica functio applica_sine_ordine(v: f32, f: functio(f32) -> f32) -> f32 poscit alloc {
    redde f(v);
}

publica functio identitas_rete(v: f32) -> f32 poscit rete {
    redde v;
}

publica functio ataca(v: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc {
    redde applica_sine_ordine(v, identitas_rete);
}

// TEST: entry=9 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0303 status=deferred needs=type_checker
